@startuml installation-and-first-run
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

' Installation from zero and the first run of the main loop: prerequisites
' (the system's git and Go, never overridden), a signed bootstrap, the keeper
' package's apiary profile installed on signed audit records (no long local
' audit), keeper init instantiating the root from a pinned template package
' (no upstream to us), the first run taking branch A (local model, after
' stating the download) or branch B (semi-automatic harness setup, asking for
' the default when none is logged in), channels, the companion app (download
' link, then pairing, each as a QR code in the terminal with a code as
' fallback), the first process and the login agent.
' Sources: main loop spec DRAFT v0.2 §6, §10.6, §11.3; curator-spec issues
' #92, #93, #94; curator issue #87; curator-inference-manager.

title Installation and first run
caption Sources: main loop DRAFT v0.2 §6, §10.6, §11.3; curator-spec #92, #93, #94; curator #87

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor $SERVICE
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $SERVICE_LINE
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $COMMITTED
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $COMMITTED_LINE

start
:Verify the installer's signature;
if (git on the system?) then (yes)
  :Use the system's git;
else (no)
  :Install a lightweight git
  (Command Line Tools on macOS or a
  Curator-managed git; never full Xcode);
endif
if (System Go inside Curator's supported range?) then (yes)
  :Use the system's Go;
else (no)
  :Curator installs its own toolchain
  in its own directory (never on PATH);
endif
:Install Curator (script from the website or Homebrew)
and verify the release signature;
:<i>curator profile install relux-works/curator-playbook-keeper</i>
(short form and default directory: profiles/apiary);
:Accept packages on signed audit records
(no long local audit; others audited or refused by policy);
:Build the commands from source (go-v1 driver);
:<i>keeper init</i>: instantiate <U+007E>/apiary from the pinned
template package (the person's own repository, no upstream),
install the system roles' profiles, initialize the board, first commit;
if (Hardware meets the published minimum?) then (yes)
  :State the download: engine and model size,
  disk space, expected time; ask the person;
  if (Person accepts?) then (yes)
    :Install the engine package and a small local model
    (curator-inference-manager);
    :Start the main loop on the local model;
    :Questionnaire: which subscriptions and harnesses?
    Add runtime bindings;
  else (no, set up a harness instead)
    :Semi-automatic harness setup
    (as in the other branch);
  endif
else (no)
  :Detect installed harnesses and logins,
  print the shortest install and login steps,
  check the result;
  if (A harness is logged in?) then (yes)
    :The first logged-in harness becomes the default;
  else (no)
    :Ask which installed harness becomes the default;
  endif
  :Start the main loop on it;
endif
:Offer channels: messengers through waggle providers
(terminal until then: <i>keeper</i>);
:Ask iOS or Android; show the app's download link
as a QR code in the terminal (or a short link);
if (Node has a screen or a terminal the person sees?) then (yes)
  :Show the pairing QR code in the terminal
  (or a pairing code);
else (headless)
  :Pair by a short code over SSH and compare the
  authentication string, or relay from a paired workstation;
endif
:Keys exchanged and pinned;
:The person asks; the main loop proposes processes
from published packages; the designer creates one;
:The person confirms (companion app or OS authentication);
:The main loop starts the process's root orchestrator;
:Register the login agent that runs <i>keeper up</i> at every login;
stop

@enduml
